r Adjustments \"Post Exposure\" Setting.\")]"]},{"t":"public FloatParameter evMin;","o":"0x40","a":["[Tooltip(\"You can clamp the lower bound of exposure values. Clamping the lower bound to a high value such as 1 will cause darker scenes to be overexposed. Refer to documentation for more detail on understanding EV values.\")]"]},{"t":"public FloatParameter evMax;","o":"0x48","a":["[Tooltip(\"You can clamp the upper bound of exposure values. Clamping the upper bound to a low value such as 5 will cause brighter scenes to be underexposed. Refer to documentation for more detail on understanding EV values.\")]"]},{"t":"public FloatParameter evCompensation;","o":"0x50","a":["[Tooltip(\"You can use the Exposure Compensation setting to adjust the baseline exposure for your shots. Exposure Compensation follows a power curve. -2 is one-fourth as bright, -1 is one-half as bright, 0 is default, +1 is twice as bright, +2 is four times as bright, and so on.\")]"]},{"t":"public TextureCurveParameter compensationCurveParameter;","o":"0x58","a":["[Tooltip(\"You can configure an additional Exposure Compensation Curve that is applied on top of the fixed Exposure Compensation setting. Your curve should at least include the range of the EV Min to EV Max values. Exposure Compensation follows a power curve. -2 is one-fourth as bright, -1 is one-half as bright, 0 is default, +1 is twice as bright, +2 is four times as bright, and so on.\")]"]},{"t":"public AutoExposureAdapationModeParameter adaptationMode;","o":"0x60","a":["[InspectorName(\"Mode\")]","[Tooltip(\"The mode that will be used to adjust exposure over time. Progressive animates the exposure over time. Instant jumps the exposure to the target value instantly.\")]"]},{"t":"public FloatParameter darkToLightSpeed;","o":"0x68","a":["[Tooltip(\"The rate (in f-stops) at which the Auto Exposure will adjust from dark to light scenes. Eyes are faster to adapt when moving from a dark to a light environment, so this value should generally be larger than the Light to Dark Speed.\")]"]},{"t":"public FloatParameter lightToDarkSpeed;","o":"0x70","a":["[Tooltip(\"The rate (in f-stops) at which the Auto Exposure will adjust from light to dark scenes. Eyes are slower to adapt when moving from a light to a dark environment, so this value should generally be smaller than the Dark to Light Speed.\")]"]},{"t":"public AutoExposureMeteringMaskModeParameter meteringMaskMode;","o":"0x78","a":["[Tooltip(\"Set whether the metering mask should be sampled from a procedural radial falloff or a texture mask (to be provided by user). Textural mode with no texture results in no metering mask being applied.\")]"]},{"t":"public TextureParameter meteringMaskTexture;","o":"0x80","a":["[Tooltip(\"A texture mask used to weight the relative importance of samples taken from various positions on screen. Automatically stretched to fit. Greyscale texture is expected and only the red channel is sampled.\")]"]},{"t":"public MinFloatParameter meteringProceduralFalloff;","o":"0x88","a":["[Tooltip(\"Controls the radial importance falloff for procedural metering masks. A higher value means that the importance decreases more rapidly as you approach the screen edges.\")]"]},{"t":"public AutoExposureRenderingModeParameter renderingMode;","o":"0x90","a":["[Tooltip(\"Set the method used to calculate and apply the auto exposure. Compute is faster and more accurate, but only works on Compute-capable systems (SM4.5+).\")]"]},{"t":"public IntParameter sampleCount;","o":"0x98","a":["[Tooltip(\"Controls the number of samples taken to estimate the screen brightness. Higher sample counts increase the performance cost.\")]"]},{"t":"public AutoExposureModeParameter animateSamplePositions;","o":"0xA0","a":["[Tooltip(\"Set to On to randomize the sample positions each frame. Creates jitter when enabled. Set to Off to use fixed sample positions. Creates sudden jumps in exposure when disabled.\")]"]},{"t":"public ClampedFloatParameter response;","o":"0xA8","a":["[Tooltip(\"Sets the temporal filtering applied to the screen brightness estimate. A higher value means that more recent samples are weighted more strongly.\")]"]},{"t":"public AutoExposureModeParameter clampingEnabled;","o":"0xB0","a":["[Tooltip(\"Set to On to enable sample clamping. Sample clamping reduces the variance of results in high-variance screen conditions at the cost of lower responsiveness and less accurate results.\")]"]},{"t":"public FloatParameter clampingBracket;","o":"0xB8","a":["[Tooltip(\"Controls the size of the clamping bracket in luminance units. A value of 1 corresponds to a bracket equal to the trailing luminance +/- 1.\")]"]}],"props":[],"methods":[{"s":"public bool IsActive()","rva":"0x4EC3D20","slot":8,"a":[]},{"s":"public bool IsTileCompatible()","rva":"0x7EB9F0","slot":9,"a":[]},{"s":"public void .ctor()","rva":"0x4EC3D50","a":[]}]},{"i":36282,"ns":"OccaSoftware.AutoExposure.Runtime","k":"c","name":"AutoExposureModeParameter","decl":"public sealed class AutoExposureModeParameter : VolumeParameter<AutoExposureMode>","attrs":["[Serializable]"],"fields":[],"props":[],"methods":[{"s":"public void .ctor(AutoExposureMode value, bool overrideState = False)","rva":"0x4EC3CC0","a":[]}]},{"i":36283,"ns":"OccaSoftware.AutoExposure.Runtime","k":"c","name":"AutoExposureAdapationModeParameter","decl":"public sealed class AutoExposureAdapationModeParameter : VolumeParameter<AutoExposureAdaptationMode>","attrs":["[Serializable]"],"fields":[],"props":[],"methods":[{"s":"public void .ctor(AutoExposureAdaptationMode value, bool overrideState = False)","rva":"0x4EBE6D0","a":[]}]},{"i":36284,"ns":"OccaSoftware.AutoExposure.Runtime","k":"c","name":"AutoExposureMeteringMaskModeParameter","decl":"public sealed class AutoExposureMeteringMaskModeParameter : VolumeParameter<AutoExposureMeteringMaskMode>","attrs":["[Serializable]"],"fields":[],"props":[],"methods":[{"s":"public void .ctor(AutoExposureMeteringMaskMode value, bool overrideState = False)","rva":"0x4E